 #uuid "5340e926-2580-5f2f-bf08-46d25e342346" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424871 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424872 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424873 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424880 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424881 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1077 "selection" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424881 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424884 1079 #uuid "ce55fccd-c2b9-544b-881d-b59a7e7c0f42" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424868 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424870 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424874 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424876 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424879 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1077 "selection" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424870 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424885 1079 #uuid "cf2e7998-6dc3-5838-ae14-0d427c2b4449" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424884 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1069 "q-89727" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{e}^{-|x/3|}}{6},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\, & x<0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1072 #uuid "2b70eaac-0c45-5da5-8a2f-2002d9071035" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424886 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{2}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{2}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{{e}^{-t/3}}{6}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x/3}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-x/3}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424885 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1069 "q-89695" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{x}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 5).$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1072 #uuid "5d72a8e6-eda0-59be-829b-e0298d5412e1" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424887 1074 "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is $F(5)=1-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{4}{5}.$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424883 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1069 "q-126156" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}(x-1)(x-4),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1072 #uuid "97c91681-ff70-5452-bbfe-e1a92bb2e9d1" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424888 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}-\\frac{2}{9}(t-1)(t-4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}-\\frac{2}{9}({t}^{2}-5t+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{2}{27}{t}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{t}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x-(-\\frac{2}{27}+\\frac{5}{9}-\\frac{8}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{27}{x}^{3}+\\frac{5}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{8}{9}x+\\frac{11}{27}, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424889 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424890 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424889 1062 #uuid "3f2429d9-8a43-540c-8ee1-21b8c07473a4" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424889 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424886 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424890 1062 #uuid "9bf4404a-eca3-5f58-9aa8-59a46fdb29aa" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424890 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424888 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424891 1058 #edb/ref 17592186424889 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424891 1062 #uuid "b81f8974-1a7b-53cb-bb5f-1b47021e293e" 13194139534538 17592186045417 true] [17592186424891 1063 #edb/ref 17592186424887 13194139534538 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-dc977e81-fd96-5729-9752-b43ae05cc6d8" 17592186424867 "answer-0d43dadc-2415-595b-83bd-07293e62a4d7" 17592186424868 "answer-27f33f1e-6e04-5ef0-8a18-a9a9635e495a" 17592186424869 "answer-2d728c61-ee7a-5242-b976-dff68318b24a" 17592186424870 "answer-492f777b-8264-55ab-9be1-d1359bd9513d" 17592186424871 "answer-4a7a5540-6762-5260-9b7f-2a98061bf95e" 17592186424872 "answer-50e4b7f0-64ef-587b-bfde-a4520b836560" 17592186424873 "answer-54302da3-4ffd-5ae6-9474-e5f95bb705f9" 17592186424874 "answer-7bc40166-55c4-53b3-bf06-562cddc8e868" 17592186424875 "answer-86635ef4-b567-5842-a8be-7564b4bc47cb" 17592186424876 "answer-8a0df617-e565-5181-bd27-09321bb7abfd" 17592186424877 "answer-a3e9b386-cf97-5734-82c8-f8b9318ea865" 17592186424878 "answer-